{
  "_comment": "How each facade-atlas tile is assembled from Downtown City MegaKit pieces (CC0, Quaternius). Order = the FACADE columns in src/assets/proceduralTextures.js. width/height = the slice of wall (metres) that becomes one tile; pieces = [kit file name, x, y, z, rotY degrees] (x = centre, metres). y0 = bottom of the slice (default 0). A tile is one bay x one floor in the game (3.2 x 3.1 m), so width 3.2 keeps proportions; 4 = a 4 m kit piece squeezed a little. tint=false keeps a material's own colour (default: wall materials are made grey so the game can tint them per building).",
